ic analysis pass between parsing and IR generation \u2014 type information is resolved structurally during the IR walk. A dedicated analysis phase is planned.' This appears to be stale relative to the current source: src/sema.psm already implements a full analyze_module semantic-analysis pass (type checking, overload resolution, move/borrow/drop checking) and src/main.psm's compile_source explicitly invokes analyze_module(merged_ast) before IR generation."}, {"id": "contributing_test_naming_convention", "label": "Test naming convention (test_<NN>_<description>.psm)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each test must be self-contained (only depends on utils.psm), exit 0 on success, and cover one scoped language behavior; the runner treats any non-zero exit as failure."}], "edges": [{"source": "contributing_semantic_analysis_claim", "target": "src_sema_analyze_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "AMBIGUOUS", "confidence_score": 0.3, "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "contributing_project_structure", "target": "src_main_main", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "contributing_project_structure", "target": "src_lexer_lex_all_tokens", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "contributing_project_structure", "target": "src_keywords_is_keyword", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "contributing_project_structure", "target": "src_parser_parse_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTE